{"tool_name":"prioritree","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"prioritree","home":"https://github.com/jsigao/prioritree","license":"Not licensed","summary":"A utility for improving phylodynamic analyses in BEAST.","addition_date":"2023-03-23T00:24:50.222589Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:51:53.805743Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:prioritree","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jsigao@ucdavis.edu","name":"Jiansi Gao","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-5108-828X","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Brian R. Moore"},{"name":"Bruce Rannala"},{"name":"Michael R. May"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data handling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2409"},{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"PrioriTree","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac849","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: Phylodynamic methods are central to studies of the geographic and demographic history of disease outbreaks. Inference under discrete-geographic phylodynamic models\u2014which involve many parameters that must be inferred from minimal information\u2014is inherently sensitive to our prior beliefs about the model parameters. We present an interactive utility, PrioriTree, to help researchers identify and accommodate prior sensitivity in discrete-geographic inferences. Specifically, PrioriTree provides a suite of functions to generate input files for\u2014and summarize output from\u2014BEAST analyses for performing robust Bayesian inference, data-cloning analyses and assessing the relative and absolute fit of candidate discrete-geographic (prior) models to empirical datasets.","authors":[{"name":"Gao J."},{"name":"May M.R."},{"name":"Moore B.R."},{"name":"Rannala B."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00Z","j